{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080504-area-spells-on-an-item","id":1080504,"title":"Area spells on an item?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-18T12:58:52-07:00","id":1080504,"title":"Area spells on an item?","content":"Is it possible to put an area spell on an item, and then carry that item around and have it be the center of the area?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T13:11:50-07:00","id":1080512,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not, there is really no difference between &quot;this bit of grass&quot; and &quot;this rock I always carry in my pocket&quot;. The spell should spread a certain amount of distance from the point of origin, no matter whether that point is defined as stationary or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 04-18-2017, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T14:10:53-07:00","id":1080547,"title":"","content":"I go with +1 Reach: Anchor the area spell on something other than the earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T21:16:45-07:00","id":1080731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080504-area-spells-on-an-item#post1080504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to put an area spell on an item, and then carry that item around and have it be the center of the area?</div> </div> </div> </div>Isnt this just an imbued item with the area spell you want on it? Otherwise id say no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T23:38:15-07:00","id":1080759,"title":"","content":"I think it would depend on what the spell does. Like if you cast Web of Life on a ring, then prior specified lifeforms that the spell is meant to detect will inform the ring when those targets enter the field--which is likely useless since the ring won't care. But maybe like a fate spell to ping you when a ping is sent to the ring might work! But something like a ring that forces the temperature of the area it is inhabiting to stay a certain temperature will follow the ring just fine? I think that would be how it would work. As long as you kept in mind that the object you enchant is the center.<br /> <br /> An imbued item would probably be better otherwise?? If I'm wrong I mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T01:00:14-07:00","id":1080774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080504-area-spells-on-an-item?p=1080731#post1080731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isnt this just an imbued item with the area spell you want on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>What projectmoon desribed isn't an Imbued Item. Imbued Items are able to cast Spells. Here, we have an item that had a Spell cast on it - very different. If that Spell were Indefinite, it could make the object an Enhanced Item, but I'm not certain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T02:41:49-07:00","id":1080794,"title":"","content":"One of my players wanted to do this, which is why I asked. My original thought was to manipulate the spell itself with Space (or maybe Space + Prime conjunctional). I also like the Reach effect; it's a simple solution. Teatime is correct, though. I'm not asking about imbued items that cast spells. Rather, I'm talking about a persistent area effect whose point of origin is something you can easily hold or move. The rules in the book seem to assume anchoring to the Earth is the way mages go about things, but I'm sure mages have thought about making magical detector devices or using Sleepers as walking spell origin points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T02:51:33-07:00","id":1080800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080504-area-spells-on-an-item?p=1080774#post1080774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What projectmoon desribed isn't an Imbued Item. Imbued Items are able to cast Spells. Here, we have an item that had a Spell cast on it - very different. If that Spell were Indefinite, it could make the object an Enhanced Item, but I'm not certain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, reread the imbued item description and attainments and may have confused it with 1e items.<br /> <br /> On thinking further absolutely not then, Imagine a stone of darkness that cast a aoe version of Deepen shadows that applies the blind tilt on everything in the area. Being able to wander with it in your hand blinding people as you go is just to good and thats just death 1. It'd get crazier if it was possible with other spells. What you'd have to do is have an imbued item cast Deepen Shadow in an area, move, recast, move recast etc. No moveable aoe spells pls.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T02:56:26-07:00","id":1080801,"title":"","content":"<br /> I find it ridiculous that mages fighting the lie would limit themselves to Earth as a reference point. We know that spell reassesses itself all the time so it s not a stretch to say that movement of the center won't hurt this ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T03:36:19-07:00","id":1080807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080504-area-spells-on-an-item?p=1080800#post1080800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, reread the imbued item description and attainments and may have confused it with 1e items.<br /> <br /> On thinking further absolutely not then, Imagine a stone of darkness that cast a aoe version of Deepen shadows that applies the blind tilt on everything in the area. Being able to wander with it in your hand blinding people as you go is just to good and thats just death 1. It'd get crazier if it was possible with other spells. What you'd have to do is have an imbued item cast Deepen Shadow in an area, move, recast, move recast etc. No moveable aoe spells pls.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you resolve aoe on a plane? Let's take the Deepen Shadows example. Will it last for a split second and then go with a wind or it will stick to its original target, shadow inside of a plane? I'm curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T03:39:09-07:00","id":1080808,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a> Also the Mage with the rock would be a moving bubble of darkness, do you think just slipping it in your pocket would turn off an effect like that? It wouldn't. It would be susceptible to Dissonance and carrying it around the Mage would be susceptible to his own darkness effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T04:31:00-07:00","id":1080817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080504-area-spells-on-an-item?p=1080807#post1080807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you resolve aoe on a plane? Let's take the Deepen Shadows example. Will it last for a split second and then go with a wind or it will stick to its original target, shadow inside of a plane? I'm curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>A spells area of effect is determined when cast and i assume part of its imago. On its own the area wont move unless confined to inside something that moves. So on a plane the area of effect is inside the plane right? so inside the plane is dark. You either cast spells on something or on an area, not on something with an area.<br /> <br /> Having AoE stuff on a area in a moving object becomes tricky if the aoe is bigger than the moving object, i can see maybe having a car imbued with &quot;deepen shadows&quot; that has a campus sized area of effect, then you could drive that around and blind stuff as it moves, but then thats not an object with a centered aoe effect thats a moveable aoe effect on its own. Something i might not allow and cap the limit of the area to inside a movable thingy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a> Also the Mage with the rock would be a moving bubble of darkness, do you think just slipping it in your pocket would turn off an effect like that? It wouldn't. It would be susceptible to Dissonance and carrying it around the Mage would be susceptible to his own darkness effect. </div> </div> </div>Well yes, the mage would also probably be blinded and yes once cast the darkness stays till its duration has ended, you could do whatever you want with the imbued item after that and yes it would be susceptible to dissonance but that wasnt the question asked. The mage isnt a moving bubble of darkness the rock would cast the spell over the area and that area becomes dark, you could take the rock outside the area of effect into a lit area and recast it to make another area centered on the stone dark but the darkess affect doesnt move with the stone, it just drops the aoe spell around it whenever it casts it and the area usually wont move. (See above with vehicles.)<br /> <br /> Say the aoe was only 1m x 1m x1m cube, the rock casts the spell and a cube of darkness happens, with the mage and rock inside, but the darkness doesnt follow the rock. The mage moves outside the cube of darkness with the rock and reuses the rock and another cube of darkness appears. He can do this as long as the item has mana, creating 1x1x1 cubes of darkness all over the place, but the cube doesnt move with the rock once cast. And i cant find evidence that its intended as such...<br /> <br /> By all means allow it, but your opening a can of worms by doing so.<br /> <br /> Rereading imbued item im also abit confused. Say i want to make a ring of invisibility, i imbue forces invisibility spell into the item, and give it to somebody. When they use it does a) the item become invis, b) the user become invis c) any subject the user/spell decides becomes invis. From reading the attainment, it seems the maker has full control over the spell till released, so i assume its up to the maker and he can change it between use? Perhaps this should go in the question thread too??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-19-2017, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T04:33:46-07:00","id":1080819,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a> I think you're conflating an Imbued Item with what the OP was talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T04:48:51-07:00","id":1080826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080504-area-spells-on-an-item?p=1080819#post1080819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a> I think you're conflating an Imbued Item with what the OP was talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>You cant do what the OP wants, but you could simulate it with a imbued item. You;d just have to recast the area spell as your about to leave the previous area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T04:58:02-07:00","id":1080831,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a> Can you give me an example of the worms in the can?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T05:18:02-07:00","id":1080838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080504-area-spells-on-an-item?p=1080831#post1080831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a> Can you give me an example of the worms in the can?</div> </div> </div> </div>Casting aoe spells on items, then teleporting said item would be a cheesy way to dodge area penalties on a sympathetic spell? Walking around turning everybody who gets close to you into a frog is also pretty good. Movable cold snap might be amusing if you can fly and avoid the cold. Obv most effects the user will get caught in it too, but one assumes they will take that into account and prepare for it. Could prob think of more but if people cant think of ways to abuse movable aoe's then or see why its a problem, go right ahead and allow it? Id love to hear how it gets abused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T05:26:11-07:00","id":1080840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080504-area-spells-on-an-item?p=1080826#post1080826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You cant do what the OP wants, but you could simulate it with a imbued item. You;d just have to recast the area spell as your about to leave the previous area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why can't you do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T05:40:08-07:00","id":1080846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080504-area-spells-on-an-item?p=1080840#post1080840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why can't you do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>When you cast a spell you choose a target or targets or an area for the spell, you dont choose a target AND area. Its one OR the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T05:46:00-07:00","id":1080848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080504-area-spells-on-an-item?p=1080838#post1080838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Casting aoe spells on items, then teleporting said item would be a cheesy way to dodge area penalties on a sympathetic spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not different from scry and remote casting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Walking around turning everybody who gets close to you into a frog is also pretty good. Movable cold snap might be amusing if you can fly and avoid the cold. </div> </div> </div> Changing people into frogs is still withstood and hubristic if any bystander gets caught in it. Hubris is good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obv most effects the user will get caught in it too, but one assumes they will take that into account and prepare for it. Could prob think of more but if people cant think of ways to abuse movable aoe's then or see why its a problem, go right ahead and allow it? Id love to hear how it gets abused. </div> </div> </div>I have played 3 months with it and I can't find anything that I would call abusing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T05:48:28-07:00","id":1080849,"title":"","content":"According to the listing of scale under page 113 of the Mage Book...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The scale of a spell is how large the spell is. Mages must decide when casting whether they are targeting specific subjects or a blanket area of effect. Aimed spells (see below) must use area of effect, centered on wherever the mage aims. </div> </div> </div>I would say that because you cannot target the item itself and apply an area of effect, then no - you are not able to anchor the area of effect to an item and move that area of effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T05:53:57-07:00","id":1080851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080504-area-spells-on-an-item?p=1080846#post1080846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you cast a spell you choose a target or targets or an area for the spell, you dont choose a target AND area. Its one OR the other.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Earth is moving around the Sun with speed of 110.000 km/h(not to mention rotation and movement of the Sun through galaxy). When you cast area spell you choose to anchor the area on the Earth. Otherwise long lasting effect would be impossible to achieve - Deepen Shadows would stay behind our planet in a blink of an eye.<br /> I get that this might be the base and most intuitive way of anchoring but I see no reason to not change it with some Reach.<br /> Area coordinates are always relative to something you chose to be a point of reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T05:57:28-07:00","id":1080853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080504-area-spells-on-an-item?p=1080851#post1080851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Earth is moving around the Sun with speed of 110.000 km/h(not to mention rotation and movement of the Sun through galaxy).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats the lie, dont fall for it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T06:00:27-07:00","id":1080855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080504-area-spells-on-an-item?p=1080846#post1080846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you cast a spell you choose a target or targets or an area for the spell, you dont choose a target AND area. Its one OR the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you pay the dice penalties for I don't see why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T06:10:57-07:00","id":1080859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080504-area-spells-on-an-item?p=1080848#post1080848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not different from scry and remote casting.<br /> <br /> Changing people into frogs is still withstood and hubristic if any bystander gets caught in it. Hubris is good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have played 3 months with it and I can't find anything that I would call abusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming you could then using the darkness stone example above, if i were to cast an area deepen shadows spell sympathetically id have to take penalties for the area but if i have an area darkness on the stone i dont need to take area penalties on the co-locate/teleport spell. Thats hugely different from scry/remote casting. What about a moveable colocate spell, i'll wander round everywhere why my gun cabinet next to me or better yet my own pocket realm (no time) meaning i can walk about and anybody i touch gets put into a frozen prison..While you or i may not be able to come up with stupid ways to abuse it im pretty sure others could hence why its not possible in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-19-2017, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T06:21:01-07:00","id":1080861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080504-area-spells-on-an-item?p=1080855#post1080855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you pay the dice penalties for I don't see why not.</div> </div> </div> </div>And thats fine, hell we should have just replied &quot;If you want to allow it then yes go ahead.&quot; then? And while often get frustrated at how Mage is written and the numerous interpretations one can have, from reading the book i think its leaning to not being allowed. Obviously Mionen has been allowing it for 3 months without a problem but i know for a fact that my players (once i convince them 2e is worth playing haha) would give me numerous headaches if i allowed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}